Here's the complete HTML document for the falling-sand cellular automata sandbox with dark theme, material buttons, and a deterministic simulation engine.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Falling Sand</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: #0d0d14;
            --surface: #1a1a28;
            --border: #2a2a3d;
            --text: #c8c8d4;
            --text-secondary: #8888a0;
            --sand: #e8c547;
            --water: #4a90d9;
            --wall: #888888;
            --acid: #5cd65c;
            --danger: #e05555;
            --highlight: #ffffff;
        }

        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            background: var(--bg);
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
            user-select: none;
            -webkit-user-select: none;
            -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
            overflow-y: auto;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 16px;
            background: var(--surface);
            border-radius: 20px;
            padding: 28px 24px 24px;
            box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5), 0 0 0 1px var(--border);
            max-width: 580px;
            width: 100%;
        }

        .title {
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: var(--text);
            letter-spacing: 0.02em;
            margin: 0;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .canvas-wrapper {
            position: relative;
            border-radius: 12px;
            overflow: hidden;
            box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--border), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
            line-height: 0;
            flex-shrink: 0;
        }

        #sand {
            display: block;
            cursor: crosshair;
            background: #1a1a2e;
            width: 500px;
            height: 500px;
            image-rendering: pixelated;
            image-rendering: crisp-edges;
        }

        .controls {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 8px;
            justify-content: center;
            width: 100%;
        }

        .material-btn {
            padding: 10px 18px;
            border-radius: 25px;
            border: 2px solid transparent;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.15s ease;
            letter-spacing: 0.03em;
            outline: none;
            position: relative;
            color: #1a1a1a;
            flex-shrink: 0;
        }

        .material-btn:hover {
            transform: translateY(-2px);
            box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
        }
        .material-btn:active {
            transform: translateY(0);
            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
        }

        .material-btn.selected {
            border-color: #ffffff;
            box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25), 0 6px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
            transform: translateY(-1px);
        }

        #mat-sand {
            background: var(--sand);
            color: #3d2e00;
        }
        #mat-water {
            background: var(--water);
            color: #fff;
        }
        #mat-wall {
            background: var(--wall);
            color: #fff;
        }
        #mat-acid {
            background: var(--acid);
            color: #0a2e0a;
        }
        #mat-empty {
            background: #3a3a4a;
            color: #ddd;
            border-style: dashed;
            border-color: #666;
        }
        #mat-empty.selected {
            border-style: solid;
            border-color: #ffffff;
        }

        #clear {
            padding: 10px 22px;
            border-radius: 25px;
            border: 2px solid var(--danger);
            background: transparent;
            color: var(--danger);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: all 0.15s ease;
            letter-spacing: 0.04em;
            outline: none;
            flex-shrink: 0;
        }
        #clear:hover {
            background: var(--danger);
            color: #fff;
            transform: translateY(-2px);
            box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(224, 85, 85, 0.35);
        }
        #clear:active {
            transform: translateY(0);
            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(224, 85, 85, 0.25);
        }

        .hint {
            font-size: 0.75rem;
            color: var(--text-secondary);
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: -4px;
        }

        @media (max-width: 560px) {
            #sand {
                width: 400px;
                height: 400px;
            }
            .container {
                padding: 16px 10px 14px;
                gap: 10px;
            }
            .material-btn {
                padding: 8px 13px;
                font-size: 0.78rem;
                border-radius: 20px;
            }
            #clear {
                padding: 8px 15px;
                font-size: 0.78rem;
            }
            .title {
                font-size: 1.2rem;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="title">Falling Sand</h1>
        <div class="canvas-wrapper">
            <canvas id="sand" width="500" height="500"></canvas>
        </div>
        <div class="controls">
            <button id="mat-sand" class="material-btn selected">Sand</button>
            <button id="mat-water" class="material-btn">Water</button>
            <button id="mat-wall" class="material-btn">Wall</button>
            <button id="mat-acid" class="material-btn">Acid</button>
            <button id="mat-empty" class="material-btn">Eraser</button>
            <button id="clear">Clear</button>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">Click &amp; drag on the canvas to paint</p>
    </div>

    <script>
        (function() {
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Grid & constants
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            const W = 100;
            const H = 100;
            const CELL_SIZE = 5;
            const CANVAS_SIZE = W * CELL_SIZE; // 500

            const EMPTY = 0;
            const SAND = 1;
            const WATER = 2;
            const WALL = 3;
            const ACID = 4;

            const MATERIAL_NAMES = ['empty', 'sand', 'water', 'wall', 'acid'];
            const NAME_TO_ID = { empty: 0, sand: 1, water: 2, wall: 3, acid: 4 };

            // Precomputed 32-bit colors (ABGR little-endian)
            const COLORS = new Uint32Array(5);
            COLORS[EMPTY] = (255 << 24) | (46 << 16) | (26 << 8) | 26; // #1a1a2e
            COLORS[SAND] = (255 << 24) | (71 << 16) | (197 << 8) | 232; // #e8c547
            COLORS[WATER] = (255 << 24) | (217 << 16) | (144 << 8) | 74; // #4a90d9
            COLORS[WALL] = (255 << 24) | (136 << 16) | (136 << 8) | 136; // #888888
            COLORS[ACID] = (255 << 24) | (92 << 16) | (214 << 8) | 92; // #5cd65c

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Grid state
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            const grid = new Array(W);
            const processed = new Array(W);
            for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
                grid[x] = new Uint8Array(H);
                processed[x] = new Int32Array(H);
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // PRNG (deterministic, seeded)
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            let prngState = 0;

            function seedPRNG(s) {
                prngState = (s | 0) >>> 0;
            }

            function rand() {
                prngState = (prngState * 1103515245 + 12345) >>> 0;
                return (prngState >>> 0) / 4294967296;
            }

            function shuffleArray(arr) {
                for (let i = arr.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
                    const j = Math.floor(rand() * (i + 1));
                    const tmp = arr[i];
                    arr[i] = arr[j];
                    arr[j] = tmp;
                }
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Global step counter
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            let globalStep = 0;

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Simulation step
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            let stepId = 0;

            function doStep() {
                stepId++;
                const sid = stepId;
                const xIndices = new Array(W);
                for (let i = 0; i < W; i++) xIndices[i] = i;

                // Process bottom-up
                for (let y = H - 1; y >= 0; y--) {
                    shuffleArray(xIndices);
                    for (let xi = 0; xi < W; xi++) {
                        const x = xIndices[xi];
                        if (processed[x][y] === sid) continue;
                        processed[x][y] = sid;
                        const mat = grid[x][y];

                        switch (mat) {
                            case SAND:
                                processSand(x, y, sid);
                                break;
                            case WATER:
                                processWater(x, y, sid);
                                break;
                            case ACID:
                                processAcid(x, y, sid);
                                break;
                            case WALL:
                            case EMPTY:
                            default:
                                break;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }

            function processSand(x, y, sid) {
                // Try straight down
                if (y + 1 < H) {
                    const below = grid[x][y + 1];
                    if (below === EMPTY) {
                        // Move down
                        grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                        grid[x][y + 1] = SAND;
                        processed[x][y + 1] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                    if (below === WATER || below === ACID) {
                        // Swap: sand sinks, liquid rises
                        grid[x][y] = below;
                        grid[x][y + 1] = SAND;
                        processed[x][y + 1] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                }
                // Blocked below — try diagonals
                if (y + 1 >= H) return;
                const leftFirst = rand() < 0.5;
                const dirs = leftFirst ? [-1, 1] : [1, -1];
                for (const dx of dirs) {
                    const nx = x + dx;
                    if (nx < 0 || nx >= W) continue;
                    const belowDiag = grid[nx][y + 1];
                    if (belowDiag === EMPTY) {
                        grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                        grid[nx][y + 1] = SAND;
                        processed[nx][y + 1] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                    if (belowDiag === WATER || belowDiag === ACID) {
                        // Swap with liquid at diagonal
                        grid[x][y] = belowDiag;
                        grid[nx][y + 1] = SAND;
                        processed[nx][y + 1] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                }
            }

            function processWater(x, y, sid) {
                // Try straight down into empty
                if (y + 1 < H && grid[x][y + 1] === EMPTY) {
                    grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                    grid[x][y + 1] = WATER;
                    processed[x][y + 1] = sid;
                    return;
                }
                // Try horizontal spread
                const leftFirst = rand() < 0.5;
                const dirs = leftFirst ? [-1, 1] : [1, -1];
                for (const dx of dirs) {
                    const nx = x + dx;
                    if (nx < 0 || nx >= W) continue;
                    if (grid[nx][y] === EMPTY) {
                        grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                        grid[nx][y] = WATER;
                        processed[nx][y] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                }
            }

            function processAcid(x, y, sid) {
                // Check below for dissolution target
                if (y + 1 < H) {
                    const below = grid[x][y + 1];
                    if (below === SAND || below === WALL) {
                        // Dissolve both
                        grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                        grid[x][y + 1] = EMPTY;
                        processed[x][y + 1] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                    if (below === EMPTY) {
                        // Fall into empty
                        grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                        grid[x][y + 1] = ACID;
                        processed[x][y + 1] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                }
                // Blocked below — try horizontal spread or dissolution
                const leftFirst = rand() < 0.5;
                const dirs = leftFirst ? [-1, 1] : [1, -1];
                for (const dx of dirs) {
                    const nx = x + dx;
                    if (nx < 0 || nx >= W) continue;
                    const side = grid[nx][y];
                    if (side === SAND || side === WALL) {
                        // Dissolve adjacent
                        grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                        grid[nx][y] = EMPTY;
                        processed[nx][y] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                    if (side === EMPTY) {
                        // Spread into empty
                        grid[x][y] = EMPTY;
                        grid[nx][y] = ACID;
                        processed[nx][y] = sid;
                        return;
                    }
                }
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Canvas & rendering
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            const canvas = document.getElementById('sand');
            const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
            const imageData = ctx.createImageData(CANVAS_SIZE, CANVAS_SIZE);
            const buf = new Uint32Array(imageData.data.buffer);

            function render() {
                for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
                    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) {
                        const color = COLORS[grid[x][y]];
                        const startIdx = y * CELL_SIZE * CANVAS_SIZE + x * CELL_SIZE;
                        for (let dy = 0; dy < CELL_SIZE; dy++) {
                            const rowStart = startIdx + dy * CANVAS_SIZE;
                            for (let dx = 0; dx < CELL_SIZE; dx++) {
                                buf[rowStart + dx] = color;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
                ctx.putImageData(imageData, 0, 0);
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Mouse / touch painting
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            let selectedMaterial = SAND;
            let isPainting = false;
            let brushRadius = 1; // paints a 3x3 area (radius 1)

            function getGridPos(e) {
                const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
                const scaleX = CANVAS_SIZE / rect.width;
                const scaleY = CANVAS_SIZE / rect.height;
                const clientX = e.touches ? e.touches[0].clientX : e.clientX;
                const clientY = e.touches ? e.touches[0].clientY : e.clientY;
                const gx = Math.floor((clientX - rect.left) * scaleX / CELL_SIZE);
                const gy = Math.floor((clientY - rect.top) * scaleY / CELL_SIZE);
                return { x: gx, y: gy };
            }

            function paintAt(gx, gy) {
                for (let dx = -brushRadius; dx <= brushRadius; dx++) {
                    for (let dy = -brushRadius; dy <= brushRadius; dy++) {
                        const nx = gx + dx;
                        const ny = gy + dy;
                        if (nx >= 0 && nx < W && ny >= 0 && ny < H) {
                            grid[nx][ny] = selectedMaterial;
                            processed[nx][ny] = 0; // allow immediate simulation
                        }
                    }
                }
            }

            function handlePointerDown(e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                isPainting = true;
                const pos = getGridPos(e);
                paintAt(pos.x, pos.y);
                render();
            }

            function handlePointerMove(e) {
                if (!isPainting) return;
                e.preventDefault();
                const pos = getGridPos(e);
                paintAt(pos.x, pos.y);
                render();
            }

            function handlePointerUp(e) {
                isPainting = false;
            }

            function handlePointerLeave(e) {
                isPainting = false;
            }

            canvas.addEventListener('mousedown', handlePointerDown);
            canvas.addEventListener('mousemove', handlePointerMove);
            canvas.addEventListener('mouseup', handlePointerUp);
            canvas.addEventListener('mouseleave', handlePointerLeave);
            canvas.addEventListener('touchstart', handlePointerDown, { passive: false });
            canvas.addEventListener('touchmove', handlePointerMove, { passive: false });
            canvas.addEventListener('touchend', handlePointerUp);
            canvas.addEventListener('touchcancel', handlePointerUp);

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Button handlers
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            const materialButtons = {
                'mat-sand': SAND,
                'mat-water': WATER,
                'mat-wall': WALL,
                'mat-acid': ACID,
                'mat-empty': EMPTY,
            };

            const allMaterialBtnEls = [];
            for (const [id, mat] of Object.entries(materialButtons)) {
                const btn = document.getElementById(id);
                allMaterialBtnEls.push(btn);
                btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    selectedMaterial = mat;
                    allMaterialBtnEls.forEach(b => b.classList.remove('selected'));
                    btn.classList.add('selected');
                });
            }

            document.getElementById('clear').addEventListener('click', () => {
                clearGrid();
                render();
            });

            function clearGrid() {
                for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {
                    grid[x].fill(EMPTY);
                    processed[x].fill(0);
                }
                stepId = 0;
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Animation loop
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            const TICKS_PER_FRAME = 2;
            let animationId = null;

            function animationLoop() {
                for (let i = 0; i < TICKS_PER_FRAME; i++) {
                    doStep();
                    globalStep++;
                }
                render();
                animationId = requestAnimationFrame(animationLoop);
            }

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Programmatic API
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            function tick(n) {
                n = Math.max(0, Math.floor(n));
                if (n === 0) return;
                seedPRNG(globalStep);
                for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                    doStep();
                    globalStep++;
                }
            }

            function get(x, y) {
                if (x < 0 || x >= W || y < 0 || y >= H) return 'empty';
                return MATERIAL_NAMES[grid[x][y]];
            }

            function set(x, y, material) {
                if (x < 0 || x >= W || y < 0 || y >= H) return;
                const id = NAME_TO_ID[material];
                if (id !== undefined) {
                    grid[x][y] = id;
                    processed[x][y] = 0;
                }
            }

            function clear() {
                clearGrid();
            }

            window.sim = {
                w: W,
                h: H,
                tick: tick,
                get: get,
                set: set,
                clear: clear,
            };

            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            // Initial render & start
            // ─────────────────────────────────────
            function initPRNGForStartup() {
                // Seed PRNG for initial animation steps
                seedPRNG(0);
            }

            initPRNGForStartup();
            render();
            animationId = requestAnimationFrame(animationLoop);

            // Log API availability
            console.log('Falling-sand sandbox ready. API available at window.sim');
            console.log('  sim.w =', W, ' sim.h =', H);
            console.log('  sim.tick(n) | sim.get(x,y) | sim.set(x,y,material) | sim.clear()');
        })();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```
### Sandbox Features

Here’s how the simulation works, what you can build, and how to control it.

**Simulation Logic & Rules**
The grid follows realistic cellular-automata rules. **Sand** falls straight down and sinks through liquids, sliding diagonally when blocked. **Water** falls and spreads horizontally when it can't go down, finding the lowest available space. **Acid** moves like water but dissolves any sand or wall it touches directly below or beside, eroding structures. **Walls** are static barriers. The engine processes cells from the bottom row up, ensuring each particle moves only one cell per step with no teleporting.

**Controls & Interaction**
The sandbox is designed for satisfying play. **Click and drag** on the canvas to paint the selected material. The **material buttons** (`#mat-sand`, `#mat-water`, `#mat-wall`, `#mat-acid`, `#mat-empty`) let you switch between elements, with a clear visual indicator for the active tool. The **Clear button** (`#clear`) instantly empties the entire grid.

**Visual & API Style**
A dark, centered layout with a high-contrast canvas makes the particles pop. The simulation runs smoothly via `requestAnimationFrame`, but also exposes a **deterministic programmatic API** on `window.sim` for testing: `sim.tick(n)` advances the simulation synchronously, `sim.get(x,y)` and `sim.set(x,y,material)` read/write individual cells, and `sim.clear()` resets the grid.
